# Enterprise SPA Architecture Rules

- Framework: Vite + React 19 + TypeScript
- Routing: TanStack Router (File-based routing via `@tanstack/router-plugin/vite`)
- Server State & Caching: TanStack Query (`@tanstack/react-query` v5 for background revalidation & SWR caching)
- Client State & Persistence: Zustand (`zustand` with `persist` middleware for LocalStorage/IndexedDB sync)
- HTTP Client & Schema Parsing: Axios + Zod (centralized HTTP instance + runtime contract parsing)
- UI Components & Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 + Shadcn UI (Radix UI primitives)
- Forms & Validation: React Hook Form + Zod
- Testing & Quality: Vitest + Playwright

- Architecture & Guidelines:
  - Do NOT suggest Next.js or React Router.
  - Pure static SPA deployment architecture (zero Node.js server dependency).
  - Place all route files in `src/routes/`.
  - Organize domain-driven modules in `src/features/`, global persistent stores in `src/stores/`, and shared UI primitives in `src/components/ui/`.
  - Keep components modular, providerless state usage, and strict with TypeScript types.
